{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review

    One enrolment application, in two columns, with the controls to decide it (Visual 1).

    The left column reads in the order of the decider's questions: the strip (the state and the
    wait), the rules a confirmation touches, the comment and the details sent, the earlier
    applications (a region shown here only without JavaScript; the rules' button opens it in a
    dialogue otherwise), what confirming does with the adjustments folded under it, and the
    message and the note. The right column is the applicant's card. Below the lg breakpoint the
    columns stack in source order, so on a phone the card follows the left column's blocks, and
    focus order follows source order everywhere.

    The form posts the queue's own contract - a formaction naming the decision, a non-empty
    userenrolments array and the session key - so every guard manage.php applies to a queue
    decision applies here too; the only extra branch is the confirmation manage.php asks for
    before a cancel from this page. The application id travels in a hidden input rather than a
    checkbox because there is only ever one, and each decision is a submit button carrying its
    own formaction value, so the button pressed is the decision taken.

    Values arrive in their plain spelling and are output through double stashes, which escape
    each exactly once. The triple-stashed exceptions each say why in the partial that holds them.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * candecide boolean - whether this reader may decide the application. False for a holder of
      enrol/apply:viewapplications alone: the page renders without the outcome, the form, the
      controls and the sticky footer
    * viewonlynotice string - what a reader who may not decide is told above the columns
    * formurl string - url the decision form posts back to
    * sesskey string - session key guarding the state change
    * userenrolmentid int - the application being decided
    * stickyfooter string - the three decisions, already rendered into a core sticky footer by
      the renderer and interpolated INSIDE this form. The footer is never moved in the DOM -
      its placement is CSS - so the submits inside it post with the rest of the form, exactly as
      the queue's own bar does
    * everything enrol_apply/review_summary, enrol_apply/review_rules, enrol_apply/review_evidence,
      enrol_apply/review_history, enrol_apply/review_outcome and enrol_apply/review_applicant
      require

    Example context (json):
    {
        "candecide": true,
        "viewonlynotice": "You can view this application but not decide it.",
        "formurl": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?userenrol=42",
        "sesskey": "Ab12Cd34Ef",
        "userenrolmentid": 42,
        "status": "Awaiting a decision",
        "statuslabel": "Status",
        "statuschipclass": "enrol_apply-statuschip-pending",
        "haswaited": true,
        "waitlabel": "Awaiting a decision for",
        "waited": "5 hours 54 mins",
        "hasapplied": true,
        "appliedon": "Applied on 06/11/26, 21:00",
        "hasrules": true,
        "rulesheading": "Rules to observe",
        "hasmeters": true,
        "meters": [
            {
                "label": "Places on this method", "isplaces": true, "count": "33 of 50", "takenpercent": 66,
                "ownpercent": 2, "barclass": "bg-warning text-dark", "after": "On confirming: 34 of 50, 16 left"
            }
        ],
        "commentlabel": "Comment",
        "hascomment": true,
        "comment": "I would like to join this course.",
        "applicantname": "Ana Souza",
        "applicantrole": "Applicant",
        "picture": "<img class=\"userpicture\" src=\"https://example.com/pix/u/f1.png\" alt=\"\">",
        "outcomeheading": "On confirming",
        "outcomesentence": "Ana Souza joins the course as <strong>Student</strong>, without a group, and <strong>is notified of the approval</strong>.",
        "writelabel": "Write to the applicant or add a note for the record",
        "writehelp": "Optional.",
        "messagelabel": "Message to the applicant",
        "notelabel": "Note for the record",
        "stickyfooter": "<div id=\"sticky-footer\"><button type=\"submit\">Confirm</button></div>"
    }
}}
{{!
    The decision form wraps the columns only for a reader who may decide. A viewer reads the same
    blocks inside a plain container instead, so the opening and closing tags are chosen twice, by
    the same flag; each rendering is balanced.
}}
{{#candecide}}
<form id="enrol_apply_review_form" class="enrol_apply-review card" method="post" action="{{formurl}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="userenrolments[]" value="{{userenrolmentid}}">
{{/candecide}}
{{^candecide}}
<div class="enrol_apply-review card">
    <div class="alert alert-info" role="status">{{viewonlynotice}}</div>
{{/candecide}}
    <div class="row enrol_apply-reviewcolumns">
        <div class="col-lg-8 enrol_apply-reviewfunnel">
            {{> enrol_apply/review_summary }}
            {{> enrol_apply/review_rules }}
            {{> enrol_apply/review_history }}
            {{> enrol_apply/review_evidence }}
            {{#candecide}}
                {{> enrol_apply/review_outcome }}
            {{/candecide}}
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-4 enrol_apply-reviewaside">
            {{> enrol_apply/review_applicant }}
        </div>
    </div>
{{#candecide}}
    {{{stickyfooter}}}
</form>
{{/candecide}}
{{^candecide}}
</div>
{{/candecide}}
